; Generated by c64-source. Edit the values here: generate keeps them.
; The switches of the build. Each switch is 0 or 1: change a value, then build again.
; The defaults give the clean program: copy protection, trainers, cheats and
; changes of a crack are 0, and the fixes of the releases are 1.
; generate adds a new switch with its default and removes a switch that the
; knowledge does not have. The build of a release does not read this file.

; Trainers: off by default
TRAINER       = 0 ; on in DERBYSHIRE_RAM. $417c-$417d. Infinite lives of Derbyshire Ram: the answer Y to INFINITE LIVES ? writes $a5 at $417c, so the DEC of the lives counter becomes an LDA. Side effect: lives stays 3, so the first-jet test at $4163 passes at each new jet, and wait_fire_to_start clears the score (run runs/trainer_score).

; Changes of a crack: off by default
CRACK_RGR     = 0 ; on in RGR. $2f80-$2f86. RGR changed the credit line of the title screen from (c)VIRGIN GAMES 1983 to (c) MIKE GAMES 1983.

; Other changes
RUN_STATE     = 0 ; on in DERBYSHIRE_RAM, RGR. $35a0-$35a7, $3710-$377b, $6000-$6000. Run state: both releases were saved from a game that had run, so these bytes hold the values that the game wrote at run time, not the values of the game file.
RUN_STATE_RGR = 0 ; on in RGR. $3150-$315f, $5ffe-$5fff. Run state that only the RGR memory dump has: game charset bytes at $3150-$315f that the game wrote, and two bytes after the code that no run reads.

; Leftovers: off by default
LEFTOVERS = 0 ; 2159 bytes in 91 files in leftovers/ that nothing uses. 1 builds them, so main.asm gives the bytes of the program. Each release has them. The loader never loads them
